## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to craft an actionable, scalable incident response for a complex streaming pipeline with multi-tenant QoS, data correctness guarantees, and real-time rollback requirements.

## Key Concepts
- Observability: per-tenant backlog metrics, distributed traces, structured logs
- Backpressure handling: tenant-aware throttling, dynamic rebalancing
- Data correctness: idempotency, exactly-once semantics, DLQ handling
- Rollback safety: canary, traffic shaping, validated resumption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-idempotent write with dedupe key
async function process(msg){
  const id = msg.id;
  if(await dedupe.has(id)) return;
  await warehouse.write(msg.payload);
  await dedupe.set(id, true, TTL);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the roll-forward vs rollback paths?
- Which metrics define success for resuming traffic, and how are tenants verified?

Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a practical reliability strategy for multi-tenant, geo-distributed services under sudden load, balancing fairness and SLA adherence.

Key Concepts

- QoS with quotas and burst budgets
- Ingress-level enforcement and sidecar orchestration
- Dynamic rate limiting and circuit breakers
- Cross-region traffic steering and graceful degradation
- Observability: SLI/SLO dashboards, latency tails, queue depth
- Rollout/rollback: staged changes, synthetic tests, rapid revert

Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, fillRate) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.fillRate = fillRate; // tokens per second
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n = 1) {
    this._inject();
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
  _inject() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.last = now;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.fillRate);
  }
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and trigger a regional SLA breach, and what would your kill-switch look like?
- What data would you surface in dashboards to operators during a flash spike?

